{title: The Stone Is Rolled Away}
{subtitle: Matthew 28:1–7}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 128}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] |
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [F] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Early on the first day of the week
The women came to see [F]the tomb
[Bb]There was an earthquake and [Eb]an angel came
And [Bb]rolled the stone [F]back from the [Bb]room
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The stone is rolled a[Eb]way, the [Bb]stone is rolled a[F]way
[Bb]He is not here, [Eb]he is risen as he said
[Bb]Come and see the place where [F]the Lord lay
The stone is rolled a[Bb]way
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
His face was like the [Eb]lightning
[Bb]His clothes were white as [F]snow
[Bb]The guards were shaking [Eb]like dead men
Go [Bb]tell his [F]friends, it's [Bb]so
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

